All working. Here's the final program:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions(JsonSerializerDefaults.Web)
{
    TypeInfoResolver = new DefaultJsonTypeInfoResolver()
};

// 1) GetTypeInfo<T>() — strongly-typed metadata
JsonTypeInfo<Person> personInfo = options.GetTypeInfo<Person>();
string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new Person("Alice", 42), personInfo);

// 2) TryGetTypeInfo<T>() — probe without throwing
var limited = new JsonSerializerOptions { TypeInfoResolver = LimitedContext.Default };

if (limited.TryGetTypeInfo<int[]>(out var arrayInfo))
    Console.WriteLine($"Found: {arrayInfo!.Type.Name}");
else
    Console.WriteLine("Not available — no exception thrown");
```

**Key points:**

| API | Returns | On failure |
|-----|---------|-----------|
| `GetTypeInfo<T>()` | `JsonTypeInfo<T>` | Throws |
| `TryGetTypeInfo<T>(out …)` | `bool` + nullable `JsonTypeInfo<T>` | Returns `false` |

The `TryGetTypeInfo<T>` variant is ideal for your "branch without catch" scenario — when the source-gen context doesn't include a type, it simply returns `false`.
